WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.640
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.455
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.755 --> 00:00:14.961
Unit twenty: Reporting Verbs. Today you will report speech with precise verbs.

4
00:00:15.261 --> 00:00:17.832
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:22.092
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:23.823
Admit.

7
00:00:24.817 --> 00:00:27.292
Admit means to say you did something bad.

8
00:00:27.883 --> 00:00:29.302
He admitted breaking it.

9
00:00:29.917 --> 00:00:32.488
Your turn. Say: Admit.

10
00:00:35.333 --> 00:00:36.125
Admit.

11
00:00:36.883 --> 00:00:37.699
Deny.

12
00:00:38.683 --> 00:00:40.753
Deny means to say it is not true.

13
00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:42.711
She denied taking it.

14
00:00:43.317 --> 00:00:45.992
Your turn. Say: Deny.

15
00:00:48.833 --> 00:00:49.776
Deny.

16
00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:51.390
Suggest.

17
00:00:52.383 --> 00:00:54.789
Suggest means to propose an idea.

18
00:00:55.383 --> 00:00:56.907
I suggested leaving.

19
00:00:57.517 --> 00:00:59.774
Your turn. Say: Suggest.

20
00:01:02.633 --> 00:01:03.495
Suggest.

21
00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:05.065
Warn.

22
00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:08.131
Warn means to tell about danger.

23
00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:10.054
He warned me not to go.

24
00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.082
Your turn. Say: Warn.

25
00:01:15.933 --> 00:01:16.679
Warn.

26
00:01:17.417 --> 00:01:18.348
Promise.

27
00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.350
Promise means to say you will do it.

28
00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:23.357
She promised to call.

29
00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.521
Your turn. Say: Promise.

30
00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:30.217
Promise.

31
00:01:30.983 --> 00:01:32.019
Refuse.

32
00:01:33.017 --> 00:01:34.772
Refuse means to say no.

33
00:01:35.383 --> 00:01:36.744
He refused to help.

34
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:40.235
Your turn. Say: Refuse.

35
00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:44.484
Refuse.

36
00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:46.321
Recommend.

37
00:01:47.317 --> 00:01:49.328
Recommend means to advise.

38
00:01:49.917 --> 00:01:51.405
I recommend resting.

39
00:01:52.017 --> 00:01:54.576
Your turn. Say: Recommend.

40
00:01:57.433 --> 00:01:58.539
Recommend.

41
00:01:59.283 --> 00:02:00.331
Accuse.

42
00:02:01.317 --> 00:02:03.990
Accuse means to say someone did something wrong.

43
00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:06.118
They accused him of lying.

44
00:02:06.717 --> 00:02:09.311
Your turn. Say: Accuse.

45
00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:13.272
Accuse.

46
00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:17.950
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:18.783 --> 00:02:22.176
Visal, report what a friend said using a precise verb.

48
00:02:23.283 --> 00:02:32.962
My friend promised to call me. Reporting verbs show the speaker's purpose, so they are more precise than said. Each verb has its own pattern.

49
00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:35.295
What are the patterns?

50
00:02:36.383 --> 00:02:54.784
Verb + to-infinitive: promise, refuse, offer. Verb + -ing: admit, deny, suggest. Verb + object + to: warn, advise, invite. Accuse someone of, blame someone for, apologise for.

51
00:02:55.883 --> 00:02:57.407
Any common mistakes?

52
00:02:58.517 --> 00:03:13.095
Suggest does not take object + to: He suggested going, not suggested me to go. Do not say apologise that. Choosing the right reporting verb makes your writing clearer and more natural.

53
00:03:14.233 --> 00:03:15.943
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:16.783 --> 00:03:20.095
Grammar focus: Reporting verbs and their patterns.

55
00:03:20.395 --> 00:03:21.698
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:22.383 --> 00:03:24.093
She promised to call me.

57
00:03:24.983 --> 00:03:26.681
He admitted breaking the window.

58
00:03:27.583 --> 00:03:29.235
They accused him of lying.

59
00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:39.582
Promise / refuse / offer + to. Admit / deny / suggest + -ing. Warn / advise + object + to. Accuse someone of + -ing. Learn each verb's pattern.

60
00:03:40.317 --> 00:03:43.875
Be careful! Don't say: He suggested me to go.

61
00:03:45.833 --> 00:03:47.763
Say: He suggested going.

62
00:03:48.063 --> 00:03:49.366
Suggest takes -ing.

63
00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:52.610
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.726
Say It Precisely.

65
00:03:55.026 --> 00:03:57.177
My friend promised to call me every week.

66
00:03:58.167 --> 00:03:59.934
The boy admitted breaking the window.

67
00:04:00.933 --> 00:04:03.444
The manager refused to change the plan.

68
00:04:04.433 --> 00:04:06.549
The doctor warned me not to eat late.

69
00:04:07.533 --> 00:04:09.858
They accused him of lying, but he denied it.

70
00:04:10.967 --> 00:04:15.073
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:15.917 --> 00:04:17.568
She blank to call me tomorrow.

72
00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:21.440
A, promised. B, admitted. C, suggested.

73
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.127
The answer is A: promised.

74
00:04:28.283 --> 00:04:30.773
He blank stealing the money. (said no)

75
00:04:31.073 --> 00:04:34.703
A, denied. B, promised. C, warned.

76
00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:40.069
The answer is A: denied.

77
00:04:41.217 --> 00:04:42.926
I blank going by train.

78
00:04:43.226 --> 00:04:47.065
A, suggested. B, refused. C, warned.

79
00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.774
The answer is A: suggested.

80
00:04:53.917 --> 00:04:55.661
Which pattern is correct?

81
00:04:55.961 --> 00:05:01.890
A, He suggested me to go.. B, He suggested going.. C, He suggested that going..

82
00:05:05.433 --> 00:05:08.362
The answer is B: He suggested going..

83
00:05:09.517 --> 00:05:12.584
According to the reading, who refused to change the plan?

84
00:05:12.884 --> 00:05:16.642
A, the manager. B, the doctor. C, the boy.

85
00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:22.165
The answer is A: the manager.

86
00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:26.541
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:27.383 --> 00:05:30.637
Report something a friend said, using a reporting verb.

88
00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:41.020
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:51.289
My friend promised to help me with my project. He suggested meeting in the library, and he warned me not to be late. These reporting verbs are more precise than said.

90
00:05:51.589 --> 00:05:53.740
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:59.288
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and reporting verbs and their patterns.

92
00:05:59.588 --> 00:06:04.074
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

93
00:06:04.374 --> 00:06:07.340
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

94
00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:10.896
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

